      "keyInsight": "We usually treat freezing water like a deadly hazard that shuts our minds down into frantic shock. But in reality, jumping into ice water acts like an instant mute button for mental noise. Wim did not seek out freezing canals because he was chasing pain or athletic glory. He stepped into icy water while drowning in profound grief and heart-wrenching emotional turmoil. When life felt overwhelming and shattered his peace, the freezing water demanded every drop of his attention. It completely silenced the chaotic spiral of his racing mind in a single second. The cold does not give your brain any spare room to fret about yesterday or worry about tomorrow. It strips away every fragile ego defense and forces absolute presence into your veins.",
