      "keyInsight": "We usually treat chronic inflammation like bad weather. We think it just happens to us. Modern medicine taught us that our deep immune defenses run on autopilot. If the system goes haywire and starts attacking our own joints, we assume we need heavy pills to pull the emergency brake. But here is the wild twist. Your body is not a sealed black box. When you flood your blood with oxygen and step into the cold, your nervous system releases a natural surge of adrenaline. This surge acts like a master switch. It quietly dials down runaway swelling and clears toxic waste from your tissues. You are not stuck waiting for external rescue. You actually have a built-in thermostat for your immune system. You simply never learned where the dial was hidden.",
